From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a buffer display cannot read is never scanned out

On virtio-gpu (virgl, Mesa 26.2) the checked engine's GPU process aborted
on its first frame on a tty:

  gbm_pixmap.cc:79] DCHECK failed: buffer_->GetFlags() & GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT.
  ui::GbmPixmap::ScheduleOverlayPlane
  ...
  viz::SkiaOutputDeviceBufferQueue::Present

`DrmThread` adds a framebuffer only to a buffer allocated or imported with
GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT, so display cannot read any other. Two paths make one:

- `OzoneImageBackingFactory::CreateSharedImageInternal` retries a failed
  SCANOUT allocation as GPU_READ, without a log. The buffer queue's
  primary plane buffers are SCANOUT allocations, so a device that cannot
  allocate one, or add its framebuffer, gets a primary plane display cannot
  read. The trace above is this path: no overlay is promoted on this
  platform, so the primary plane is the only one scheduled.
- Patch 0005 imports a client's buffer without scanout when its modifier is
  render-only. It reaches a plane only through overlay promotion, which is
  off here: `supports_overlays` is false and nothing passes
  `--enable-hardware-overlays`. With it on, off ChromeOS the validator
  tests a fresh scanout buffer rather than the candidate's own
  (`allow_sync_and_real_buffer_page_flip_testing`), so it would let one
  through.

Without DCHECKs, `ScheduleOverlayPlane` queues nothing and returns true.
The commit then has no planes, and `HardwareDisplayController` ACKs
without a page flip: the screen keeps the modeset buffer and the log is
clean.

So `ScheduleOverlayPlane` keeps that behavior without the DCHECK, and logs
such a buffer's format, size and modifier once. It does not fail the frame:
SWAP_FAILED loses the context on every frame, which can loop GPU-process
restarts.

This does not make virgl draw. Why its SCANOUT allocation fails needs a
log from the machine: `--vmodule=gbm_wrapper=1,drm_framebuffer=4` shows a
failed `gbm_bo_create` or `AddFramebuffer2`.

Not reproduced; nothing here runs virgl. `GbmPixmapScanoutTest` covers the
skip and the single log.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn          |  1 +
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.cc | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.h  |  4 ++++
 3 files changed, 22 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
index b7897f32..db4abf9f 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
@@ -272,6 +272,7 @@
     "domicile/drm_sleep_unittest.cc",
     "domicile/drm_vt_switcher_unittest.cc",
     "domicile/edid_name_unittest.cc",
+    "domicile/gbm_pixmap_scanout_unittest.cc",
 
     # evdev's, not this platform's: `//ui/events/ozone/evdev:unittests` is
     # linked only into `events_unittests`, which no job here builds, and the
diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.cc b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.cc
index 3afd12cb..5dca5402 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.cc
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.cc
@@ -8,8 +8,9 @@
 #include <memory>
 #include <utility>
 
-#include "base/check.h"
+#include "base/logging.h"
 #include "ui/gfx/gpu_fence.h"
+#include "ui/gfx/linux/drm_util_linux.h"
 #include "ui/gfx/native_pixmap_handle.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/drm_overlay_plane.h"
 #include "ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_surface_factory.h"
@@ -76,7 +77,21 @@
     gfx::AcceleratedWidget widget,
     const gfx::OverlayPlaneData& overlay_plane_data,
     gfx::GpuFenceHandle acquire_fence) {
-  DCHECK(buffer_->GetFlags() & GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT);
+  // DOMICILE: a buffer allocated or imported without GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT has
+  // no framebuffer, so display cannot read it. `OzoneImageBackingFactory`
+  // makes one for the primary plane when a scanout allocation fails, and
+  // patch 0005 imports a client's buffer for sampling only. Queue no plane and
+  // say so once. Failing the frame instead loses the context every frame,
+  // which can loop GPU-process restarts.
+  if (!(buffer_->GetFlags() & GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT)) {
+    LOG_IF(ERROR, !reported_no_scanout_)
+        << "Not scanning out a " << DrmFormatToString(buffer_->GetFormat())
+        << " buffer (" << buffer_->GetSize().ToString() << ", modifier "
+        << buffer_->GetFormatModifier()
+        << ") allocated or imported without GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT";
+    reported_no_scanout_ = true;
+    return true;
+  }
   // |framebuffer_id| might be 0 if AddFramebuffer2 failed, in that case we
   // already logged the error in GbmBuffer ctor. We avoid logging the error
   // here since this method might be called every pageflip.
diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.h b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.h
index 5abd0332..7e606f1e 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.h
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/gpu/gbm_pixmap.h
@@ -56,6 +56,10 @@
   const raw_ptr<GbmSurfaceFactory> surface_manager_;
   const std::unique_ptr<GbmBuffer> buffer_;
   const scoped_refptr<DrmFramebuffer> framebuffer_;
+
+  // DOMICILE: whether `ScheduleOverlayPlane` has logged that this buffer has
+  // no GBM_BO_USE_SCANOUT.
+  bool reported_no_scanout_ = false;
 };
 
 }  // namespace ui
